# A Claude Code user opens an existing, untrusted repo that has no
# CLAUDE.md yet: trust dialog, /help, /init, /memory, then a small real
# task. kiln has no "#" memory-note shortcut (Claude Code's own reference
# source has none either - only a bash prefix and a plain prompt), so this
# no longer exercises one; a line starting with "#" is an ordinary prompt.
@real
@untrusted
@home scratch
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/ext-onboarding
@env EDITOR=true

WAITFOR /Accessing workspace/ 30
SHOT trust-dialog
KEY 2
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SEND /help
WAIT 1
SHOT help-palette
EXPECT /init/
TURN /init
RUN test -f {PROJ}/CLAUDE.md
SHOT after-init
SEND /memory
WAIT 1
SHOT memory-command
TURN Add a -version flag to the CLI that prints "greeter v1.0" and exit.
SHOT task-done
